RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3699708Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3709806Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3811867Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3822550Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3823346Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3823912Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3824174Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3825612Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3826197Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3826654Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3826991Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3827673Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3827995Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3828626Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3829532Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3830038Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3830384Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3830545Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3830721Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3830988Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3831192Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3831587Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3831741Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3831839Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3832023Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3832399Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3832864Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3837475Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3837760Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3838271Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3838596Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3839328Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3840008Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3840565Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3840835Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3841094Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3841477Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3841836Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3854222Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3855263Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3866681Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3867228Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3867648Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3868944Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3869523Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3889371Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3890036Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3901760Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3902463Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3903190Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3903532Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3903831Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3904297Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3904887Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3905686Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T20:51:36.3906088Z 
